msgid "**Setup Function**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/06-fun_Heart_rate_monitor.rst:87
msgid "Initializes I2C communication, starts serial communication, initializes the OLED display, and sets up the MAX30102 sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/06-fun_Heart_rate_monitor.rst:97
msgid "**Main Loop**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/06-fun_Heart_rate_monitor.rst:99
msgid "The core functionality resides here. The IR value is read from the sensor. If a finger is detected (IR value greater than 50,000), the program checks if a heartbeat is sensed. When a heartbeat is detected, the OLED screen displays the BPM and the time between heartbeats is used to calculate BPM. Otherwise, it prompts the user to place their finger on the sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/06-fun_Heart_rate_monitor.rst:101
msgid "We have also prepared two bitmaps with heartbeats, and by switching between these two bitmaps, we can achieve a dynamic visual effect."
msgstr ""
